course: dictionary
lesson: 3107
title: The short word el
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «El» is a very short word, and it is easy to miss what it means. Look at the words around it to find out. Most often you will meet it inside a name, not as a word on its own.
explain: «El» can be the name of the letter L, said like "ell". In Spanish, «el» means "the", as in «El Paso» and «El Niño». So when you see «El» at the start of a Spanish name, it is probably just the word "the" in another language.
explain: In Chicago, people call their raised train line «the El». The context helps here: a train on a raised track above the street is the El, not a letter. When you are not sure, read on, then check the meaning in a dictionary.
fact: «El» is the name of the letter L, said like "ell".
fact: In Spanish, «el» means «the» before a masculine noun, as in «El Paso» and «El Salvador».
fact: In the USA, «the El» is an elevated railway, a train on a raised track above the street, especially in Chicago.
fact: «El Niño» is a change in the Pacific Ocean that makes the weather unusual around the world.
fact: «El» is not an English word, so it is one to check when you meet it in a text.
exercise: What letter of the alphabet is «el» the name of? | *L | K | N | M
exercise: «El Niño is a pattern every few years in which the eastern tropical Pacific becomes unusually warm.» What is El Niño? | *A change in the Pacific Ocean that makes the weather unusual around the world | A famous train in Chicago | A ship that passes through a narrow sea | A kind of Spanish food
exercise: In Spanish, what does «el» mean in the name «El Paso»? | a | *the | is | and
test: In Chicago, what is «the El»? | A kind of bus | *An elevated railway, a train on a raised track above the street | A dish of sweetcorn | A river that flows into the Pacific
test: Why does «El» in «El Paso» not mean the letter L? | Because it is short | *Because it is a Spanish word meaning "the" | Because it is always a train | Because it means "water"
exam: Read «The Bab-el-Mandeb, between Yemen and the Horn of Africa, is about 30 km wide and links the Red Sea to the Gulf of Aden.» What is the Bab-el-Mandeb? | A famous train in Chicago | A Spanish word for "the" | A dry desert in Sudan | *A narrow sea passage between Yemen and Africa
